%!PS-Adobe-3.0
%%Title: typewriter specimen -- the /Typewriter font, from no variation to a battered machine (issues #211, #212)
%%BoundingBox: 0 0 612 792
%%EndComments

% Specimen for lib/typewriter.ps (docs/TYPEWRITER.md). Top to bottom:
%
%   ascii      the full printable ASCII set four times, with the same
%              machine and document: no variation in flat ink (/Wear 0,
%              /InkModel false: #211's ink), then in ribbon ink the
%              machine's quirks only, quirks plus line and strike variation
%              at the measured defaults (/Wear 1), and a battered machine
%              (/Wear 2.5)
%   repeats    one key struck again and again, enlarged 3.2x: with quirks
%              only every strike is the same, ink and all (a key's bias
%              holds); with strikes on, no two are alike; machine 7's `o`
%              has a clogged counter
%   presets    the same sentence on the /electric, /manual and /worn
%              presets and on a bone-dry ribbon, then elite pitch, then a
%              red ribbon run and a strikeover (a t struck over a mistyped
%              r, strike index 1)
%
% The ink is #212's ribbon ink: the weave's voids, a feathered edge,
% clogged counters, heavy sides, density from pressure and /Ribbon.
% docs/typewriter/ink_vs_real.png (docs/typewriter/tools/ink_compare.py)
% sets it beside the reference scans at their own resolution.
%
%   pscat --page 612x792 --dpi 200 --png typewriter_specimen.png examples/typewriter_specimen.ps
%   gs -q -dNOSAFER -dBATCH -dNOPAUSE -sDEVICE=png16m -r200 -dGraphicsAlphaBits=4 -dTextAlphaBits=4 \
%      -sOutputFile=typewriter_specimen_gs.png examples/typewriter_specimen.ps </dev/null

(lib/typewriter_outlines.ps) run
(lib/typewriter.ps) run

0.98 0.97 0.94 setrgbcolor clippath fill

% sp- prefix: specimen-local.
/splabel { 0.45 0.43 0.40 setrgbcolor /Helvetica findfont 7.5 scalefont setfont moveto show } def
/sprule { 0.80 0.78 0.74 setrgbcolor 0.5 setlinewidth newpath dup 54 exch moveto 558 exch lineto stroke } def

/spascii1 ( !"#$%&'\(\)*+,-./0123456789:;<=>?@ABCDEFGHIJKLMNO) def
/spascii2 (PQRSTUVWXYZ[\\]^_`abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz{|}~) def

% y opts label -   (the ASCII set on two lines at y, with opts)
/sprow {
    /splab exch def /spopt exch def /spy exch def
    splab 54 spy 11 add splabel
    72 spy moveto spopt tw-setup spascii1 show
    72 spy 12 sub moveto spascii2 show
} def

(/Typewriter -- lib/typewriter.ps, issues #211 and #212) 54 762 splabel
(Courier Prime outlines; machine 7, document 3; pica, /Size 12.5) 54 752 splabel

735 sprule
(1. No variation, flat ink \(/Wear 0, /InkModel false\): the plain face with the ink spread past it.) 54 718 splabel
72 706 moveto << /Machine 7 /Seed 3 /Wear 0 /LineWear 1 /StrikeWear 1 /MachineWear 1 /InkModel false >> tw-setup spascii1 show
72 694 moveto spascii2 show

660 << /Wear 1 /LineWear 0 /StrikeWear 0 /InkModel true >>
(2. Ribbon ink from here on. Machine quirks only: each key's own offset, lean, weight and clog, the same wherever struck.) sprow
614 << /LineWear 1 /StrikeWear 1 >>
(3. Quirks + line + strike variation at the measured defaults, /Wear 1. Real typing is this subtle.) sprow
568 << /Wear 2.5 >>
(4. A battered machine, /Wear 2.5.) sprow

540 sprule
(Repeats, enlarged 3.2x \(/Size 40, /Pitch 3.125\), /Wear 1: one key struck twelve times.) 54 524 splabel
(Quirks only) 54 500 splabel
120 490 moveto << /Wear 1 /LineWear 0 /StrikeWear 0 /Size 40 /Pitch 3.125 >> tw-setup (eeeeeeeeeeee) show
(+ strikes) 54 450 splabel
120 440 moveto << /LineWear 1 /StrikeWear 1 >> tw-setup (eeeeeeeeeeee) show
(+ strikes, o: clogged) 54 400 splabel
120 390 moveto << >> tw-setup (oooooooooooo) show

365 sprule
/spline (In reply to your letter of June 22, I will say that if you do not) def
(Presets: /electric, /manual \(the default\), /worn; then /manual on a bone-dry ribbon, /Ribbon 0.1) 54 348 splabel
72 334 moveto << /Preset /electric /Size 12.5 /Pitch 10 /Seed 11 >> tw-setup spline show
72 322 moveto << /Preset /manual >> tw-setup spline show
72 310 moveto << /Preset /worn >> tw-setup spline show
72 298 moveto << /Preset /manual /Ribbon 0.1 >> tw-setup spline show

(Elite: /Pitch 12, /Size 11.5) 54 286 splabel
72 274 moveto << /Preset /manual /Pitch 12 /Size 11.5 /Seed 12 >> tw-setup
(this exhibit until schools open, we may be able to have some specimens for) show
72 262 moveto (exhibit at the Mitchell Corn Palace. I am sorry we did not know about it.) show

(A red ribbon run \(/Ink, tw-set\), and a strikeover: a mistyped r corrected by striking t over it at /Strike 1) 54 238 splabel
72 226 moveto << /Pitch 10 /Size 12.5 /Seed 13 >> tw-setup (Please note the ) show
<< /Ink [0.62 0.12 0.10] >> tw-set (DEADLINE) show
<< /Ink [0.13 0.13 0.15] >> tw-set ( of July 1.) show
72 214 moveto (Shipped on the ten) show
currentpoint (r) show moveto << /Strike 1 >> tw-set (t) show
<< /Strike 0 >> tw-set (h, by rail.) show

190 sprule
(The same /Machine and /Seed type the same page in pscat and Ghostscript; the caller's rand stream is untouched.) 54 172 splabel
(Glyphs are drawn under setcharwidth, never cached: every strike is drawn afresh.) 54 162 splabel

showpage
